{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1550097-how-important-are-legacies-to-you","id":1550097,"title":"How important are legacies to you?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-13T06:54:34-07:00","id":1550097,"title":"How important are legacies to you?","content":"Thinking about CoD &amp; MtAw again I noticed that I find Legacies to be much more interesting than Orders. Orders feel like they are mostly useful as ties into a political setting. Which has all the problems of the new mages being at the bottom of the political heap. Legacies, on the other hand, seem to fit much more into what the new characters want to do giving the player more agency and reason to act in the world.<br /> <br /> Do most groups plan out all of the legacies they want their characters involved in at character creation? Do you put the initial initiation as part of creation or is it generally an in game character beat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-13T08:29:21-07:00","id":1550099,"title":"","content":"The one game of Mage: the Awakening I played, the Storyteller treated legacies like secret societies. We had to discover their existence and nature through in game play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-13T10:37:49-07:00","id":1550100,"title":"","content":"When I make a character, I normally plan towards a Legacy. It's a way to figure out my character's specialty, something they focus on that synergizes with their themes, and provide flavorful incentives to reinforce them (organization, yantras, oblations, traditions, etc).<br /> <br /> Orders are worldwide conspiracies, giant institutions and you are only seeing one limb of it wherever you start. Legacies tends to be more personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T03:13:26-07:00","id":1550105,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't really use them. To me they always seem a bit too inflexible; like, there's a huge amount of neat ideas and philosophies in legacies, but the system requires you to pick one and then stick to it. (That's not to say there aren't good game design reasons for that.)<br /> <br /> Also, I find the attainment system a bit too complex for the payoff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T14:44:19-07:00","id":1550118,"title":"","content":"Interesting. One of the reasons I love legacies is, as KaiserAfini says, they are personal. Otherwise I find that mages start blurring together. There is a mechanical issue in that they aren't balanced at all and some mages don't really have any legacy that fits their philosophy, path, and order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}